%# ABOUTME: /terms: the platform's terms of service, the same on the apex and every tenant host.
%# ABOUTME: perigrin's text, effective 2026-11-26; Registry::Terms::VERSION names it and bookings record it.
% layout 'default';
% title 'Terms of Service';

<article class="card" data-terms-version="<%= $terms_version %>">
    <div class="card-body">
        <p><strong>Effective November 26, 2026. Version <%= $terms_version %>.</strong></p>

        <p>These terms govern your use of Registry, the booking and registration
        service operated by Tamarou LLC, a New Mexico limited liability company
        ("Tamarou", "we", "us"), at tinyartempire.com and at every studio's own
        address on it. By creating an account, booking, or running a studio on
        Registry, you agree to them.</p>

        <h2>1. Who is who</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Studios</strong> are the businesses that sell classes, camps,
            programs and bookings through Registry. Each studio is a customer of Tamarou.</li>
            <li><strong>Customers</strong> are the people who book with a studio:
            parents, guardians, and students.</li>
            <li><strong>Tamarou</strong> provides the software. Tamarou is not the seller
            of any class, camp or booking, and is not a party to the agreement between a
            studio and its customers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Buying from a studio</h2>
        <p>When you book, you are buying from the studio, not from Tamarou.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>The studio is the merchant.</strong> Your payment is charged
            directly on the studio's own Stripe account, and the studio's name appears as
            the seller. Questions about a charge, a class, or a refund go to the studio first.</li>
            <li><strong>The studio sets its own terms.</strong> Each offer shows its price
            and its own rules for refunds, changes, and expiry before you pay. Those rules
            are part of your agreement with the studio. Read them before you book.</li>
            <li><strong>Seats are held while you pay.</strong> When you choose a time,
            Registry holds your seats for a short while. If the hold lapses before payment
            completes, the seats are released and you can start a new booking.</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic returns.</strong> If a payment arrives after its hold
            lapsed and the seats are no longer free, or if the amount paid does not match
            the price, the payment is returned to your card automatically and no booking is
            made. Returns can take 5 to 10 business days to appear.</li>
            <li><strong>Refunds and disputes.</strong> Any other refund is the studio's
            decision, under the terms of the offer you bought, and is issued by the studio.
            If you dispute a charge with your card issuer, the outcome Stripe reports is
            applied to your booking.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Running a studio on Registry</h2>
        <p>If you run a studio on Registry, these further terms apply to you.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Your plan.</strong> On signup you accept a Tamarou offer. Today the
            only offer is Solo: no monthly fee, plus 2.5% of each sale processed through
            Registry, including change fees. The terms of the offer you accepted, as shown
            when you accepted it, govern what you pay.</li>
            <li><strong>How the fee is collected.</strong> The 2.5% is taken as a Stripe
            application fee on each charge to your customers. You need a Stripe account
            connected to Registry to take payments, and you are bound by Stripe's own terms.</li>
            <li><strong>You are the merchant of record.</strong> You are responsible for
            your offers, your prices, your refund and change rules, delivering what you
            sell, taxes on your sales, and complying with the law that applies to your
            business. Stripe fees, refunds, chargebacks and dispute fees fall on your
            account as Stripe places them.</li>
            <li><strong>The fee on refunds.</strong> When you refund a sale, Tamarou keeps
            its 2.5%, unless the sale was wrong because of a Registry fault, in which case
            Tamarou returns its fee for that sale.</li>
            <li><strong>Your data and your customers' data.</strong> You keep ownership of
            your data and your customers' data. Tamarou processes it only to run Registry
            for you, and keeps each studio's data separate from every other studio's.</li>
            <li><strong>Your account.</strong> Keep your sign-in secure. Only your admins
            can publish offers and set prices.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Using Registry</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Don't misuse Registry: no attempts to reach another studio's data,
            interfere with the service, or use it for anything unlawful.</li>
            <li>You must be 18 or older to create an account. A parent or guardian books
            on a child's behalf.</li>
            <li>We may suspend an account that breaks these terms or puts other users at
            risk, and will tell you why where the law allows.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms. When we do, the version and effective date above
        change, and you are asked to agree again before your next booking. Each booking
        records the version you agreed to.</p>

        <h2>6. Warranties and liability</h2>
        <p>Registry is provided "as is". To the extent the law allows, Tamarou is not
        liable for indirect or consequential losses, and its total liability to you is
        limited to the greater of the fees Tamarou received from you in the twelve months
        before the claim, or $100. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under
        consumer law that cannot be waived.</p>

        <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, and disputes
        are heard in the state or federal courts located in Florida.</p>

        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>Tamarou LLC · 429 Hoffer Ave., Orlando, FL 32809 ·
        <a href="mailto:registry@tamarou.com">registry@tamarou.com</a></p>
    </div>
</article>
